-- title:
--   Module-finiteness of S/hS over a henselian valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring which is a domain, a valuation ring and a henselian local ring, with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_A$ (written `maximalIdeal A`). Let $B$ be a commutative $A$-algebra of finite presentation, and let $\mathfrak n \subseteq B$ be a prime ideal whose contraction along $A \to B$ is exactly $\mathfrak m_A$. Let $S$ be a commutative ring carrying $A$- and $B$-algebra structures forming a scalar tower, such that $S$ is a localisation of $B$ at the prime $\mathfrak n$, and assume $S$ is flat as an $A$-module. Let $h, T \in S$, with $T$ not a unit, and assume that the image of $h$ in $S/\mathfrak m_A S$ (where $\mathfrak m_A S$ denotes the ideal of $S$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_A$) is a non-zero-divisor, and that the quotient of $S$ by the ideal $hS + \mathfrak m_A S$ is a finite $A$-module. The conclusion is twofold: first, $S/hS$ is a finite $A$-module; second, there is a natural number $k$ such that the $k$-th power of the image of $T$ in $S/hS$ lies in the ideal of $S/hS$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_A$.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra input for a Weierstrass-preparation argument: the case of Zariski's main theorem saying that an algebra essentially of finite type over a henselian local ring which is quasi-finite at its closed point is module-finite, together with the nilpotence of a non-unit coordinate on the closed fibre. It is applied in the analysis of curves at points of the smooth locus where a coordinate has order one, namely in [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_monic_eval2_eq_mul_of_inv_mem_integers_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_monic_eval2_eq_mul_of_inv_mem_integers_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus) and [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus), and its proof invokes [`HenselianLocalRing.moduleFinite_localizationAtPrime_of_moduleFinite`](thm.html#HenselianLocalRing.moduleFinite_localizationAtPrime_of_moduleFinite).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HenselianLocalRing_moduleFinite_quotient_span_and_exists_pow_mem_of_isLocalizationAtPrime_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors.lean

